<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P affirms IBJ, LTCB ratings after tax reassessed.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P affirms IBJ, LTCB ratings after tax reassessed.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp said it had affirmed its debt ratings for Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd and Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan Ltd after both banks announced that their tax payments for fiscal 1995 had been reassessed by the authorities.  </p>
<p>Although the gross amount of extra taxes for each bank is fairly large, the net financial impact on both banks is expected to be minimal because they can realise tax deductions that were not permitted for fiscal 1995/96 in later years, it said.</p>
<p>S&amp;P affirmed the following ratings of IBJ and LTCB and their related entities, and at the same time said the outlook of the ratings was negative.</p>
<p>IBJ and its related entities:</p>
<p>	A    long-term senior debt rating</p>
<p>	     long-term counterparty rating</p>
<p>	     long-term certificate of deposit (CD) rating</p>
<p>	A-   subordinated debt rating</p>
<p>	A1   short-term CD rating</p>
<p>	     short-term counterparty rating</p>
<p>	     commercial paper rating</p>
<p>LTCB and its related entities:</p>
<p>BBB+ long-term senior unsecured debt rating</p>
<p>	     long-term counterparty rating</p>
<p>	     long-term CD rating</p>
<p>	A2   short-term CD rating</p>
<p>	     short-term counterparty rating</p>
<p>	     commercial paper rating</p>
</text>
